---
import Icon from '../components/home/Icon.astro';
import TravelGuideLayout from '../layouts/TravelGuideLayout.astro';
import { travelSources as s } from '../data/travel';
const sections = [
  { id: 'routes', label: '01 / Air routes' },
  { id: 'connections', label: '02 / Before booking' },
  { id: 'arrival', label: '03 / On arrival' },
  { id: 'onward', label: '04 / Beyond the airport' },
];
---
<TravelGuideLayout page="getting-here" title="Getting to Pohnpei | Flights, Connections & Arrival"
  description="Plan your journey to Pohnpei: United and Nauru Airlines route guidance, current schedules, connection checks, airport pickup, and onward travel."
  heading="Across the Pacific." emphasis="Into Pohnpei."
  intro="Start with the flight into Pohnpei, then build the rest of your journey around it. A little coordination between your airline, your host, and your guide makes room for the island itself."
  sections={sections}>
  <div slot="aside"><p class="tg-eyebrow">Your destination</p><h2 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-3">Three letters: PNI.</h2><p class="text-sm text-basalt/80 leading-relaxed">Search for Pohnpei International Airport. It sits on Deketik, linked to the main island by a causeway near Kolonia.</p><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href={s.airport}>FSM Civil Aviation airport guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p></div>

  <section id="routes" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright">
    <div class="tg-wrap">
      <div class="tg-split mb-10"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">01 / Air routes</p><h2 class="tg-title">Choose your<br /><em>Pacific connection.</em></h2></div><div class="tg-copy"><p>Guam and Honolulu are United’s gateways to Pohnpei. From Australia and the South Pacific, check Nauru Airlines’ network through Brisbane and Nauru. Intermediate stops and operating dates depend on the service you select.</p><p>These are route-planning starting points. Search your complete outward and return journey with the airline before committing to a stay.</p><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href={s.tourismArrival}>Pohnpei Tourism Office’s route overview <Icon name="arrow" /></a></p></div></div>
      <div class="border-y border-basalt/25">
        <article class="grid md:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.3fr_1fr] gap-6 md:gap-10 py-8">
          <div><p class="tg-eyebrow">United Airlines</p><h3 class="font-headline text-4xl">Guam /<br />Honolulu</h3></div>
          <div class="tg-copy"><p>The Island Hopper connects Guam and Honolulu through Micronesia, including Pohnpei. It is a journey with island stops; a listed connection to PNI does not necessarily mean a nonstop flight.</p><p>For travel from Asia, explore connections through Guam. From the United States, compare itineraries through Honolulu or Guam.</p></div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-3"><a href={s.united} class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon">Search United flights <Icon name="arrow" /></a><a href={s.unitedNetwork} class="tg-page-link tg-link text-sm">United’s Guam route schedules <Icon name="arrow" /></a><p class="text-xs text-basalt/75 leading-relaxed">Use your travel dates in the booking search to confirm stops, connections, and availability.</p></div>
        </article>
        <article class="grid md:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.3fr_1fr] gap-6 md:gap-10 py-8 border-t border-basalt/20">
          <div><p class="tg-eyebrow">Nauru Airlines</p><h3 class="font-headline text-4xl">Brisbane /<br />Pacific islands</h3></div>
          <div class="tg-copy"><p>Nauru Airlines publishes a regional network through Nauru (also called Naoero), with Pohnpei included in selected schedule periods. A Brisbane–Pohnpei itinerary can involve several island stops.</p><p><strong class="text-basalt">Check that Pohnpei appears in the schedule covering your dates, in both directions.</strong> Do this before arranging your flight to Brisbane or another connecting island.</p></div>
          <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-3"><a href={s.nauruSchedule} class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon">Check Nauru Airlines schedules <Icon name="arrow" /></a><p class="text-xs text-basalt/75 leading-relaxed">The airline’s schedule page also links to its booking service. Timetables are subject to change.</p></div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="connections" class="tg-section bg-sand">
    <div class="tg-wrap tg-split">
      <div><p class="tg-eyebrow">02 / Before booking</p><h2 class="tg-title">Check the whole<br /><em>journey.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">A workable flight into Pohnpei is only one part of the plan. Put every leg, overnight, and transfer on the same itinerary before you book.</p><a class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon mt-6" href="/travel-info#entry">Entry &amp; document checklist <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
      <dl class="tg-rows tg-copy">
        <div><dt>Dates, stops &amp; overnight connections</dt><dd>Read the local arrival date on every segment, especially when crossing the International Date Line. Pohnpei uses UTC +11 year-round. Check both directions for overnight layovers and leave time before a fixed tour or event.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Transit permission</dt><dd>Check the requirements for every place you pass through, including Guam or Honolulu. Permission to enter the FSM does not settle another country’s transit requirements. Start with <a class="tg-link" href={s.usTransit}>U.S. transit guidance</a> for a U.S. connection, and confirm your itinerary with the airline.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Tickets, baggage &amp; assistance</dt><dd>Ask whether your connections share one ticket, whether baggage is checked through, and what happens if a flight changes. Confirm baggage allowances and arrangements for surfboards, dive gear, mobility aids, or airport assistance before paying.</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Your first night</dt><dd>Send your host the flight number and local arrival date. Agree on pickup, a meeting point, the charge, and a phone contact. If a connection changes, update the host and your guide as well as the airline.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="arrival" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright">
    <div class="tg-wrap tg-split">
      <div><p class="tg-eyebrow">03 / On arrival</p><h2 class="tg-title">From the terminal<br /><em>to your first night.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">Keep your arrival details where you can read them without an internet connection.</p></div>
      <div>
        <ol class="tg-rows tg-copy list-none">
          <li><h3>01 / Have your documents ready</h3><p>Carry your passport, onward itinerary, and accommodation details. Complete the arrival declarations provided by your carrier or border officials. Read the <a class="tg-link" href={s.entry}>FSM entry and quarantine guidance</a> before packing plants, animals, or other restricted items.</p></li>
          <li><h3>02 / Meet your arranged transport</h3><p>Use the meeting instructions agreed with your host or driver. Taxis and rental cars are available on Pohnpei; ask your accommodation to help arrange transport and confirm the fare before the trip.</p></li>
          <li><h3>03 / Settle in &amp; plan tomorrow</h3><p>Confirm your next pickup and how to contact your host while you’re out. Check your cash and phone arrangements before heading farther from town. Our <a class="tg-link" href="/travel-info#daily-essentials">daily essentials</a> cover both.</p></li>
        </ol>
        <div class="tg-note tg-copy mt-5"><h3 class="font-headline text-2xl text-basalt mb-2">Remember the journey home.</h3><p>Ask your airline or the tourism office about the current airport departure fee and payment method, and keep enough cash aside. Published tourism sources give different amounts, so confirm it for your trip.</p><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href={s.tourismEssentials}>Pohnpei visitor information</a> · <a class="tg-link" href={s.entry}>FSM entry information</a></p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="onward" class="tg-section bg-basalt text-sand">
    <div class="tg-wrap grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 md:gap-20">
      <div><p class="text-xs tracking-[.18em] uppercase text-sand/75 mb-5">04 / Beyond the airport</p><h2 class="font-headline text-4xl md:text-5xl leading-tight mb-5">Find your base.<br /><em>Meet the island.</em></h2><p class="text-sand/85 leading-relaxed">Compare accommodation by area and published amenities, then contact a property about your dates and arrival.</p><a href="/places-to-stay" class="tg-button bg-sand text-basalt hover:bg-sand-bright mt-7">Find a place to stay <Icon name="arrow" /></a><a href="/travel-info" class="block py-5 underline underline-offset-4 text-sm">Prepare with Travel Essentials <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
      <div class="border-t border-sand/30 pt-6"><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Heading to an outer island?</h3><p class="text-sand/85 leading-relaxed mb-5">Arrival at PNI brings you to Pohnpei’s main island. Outer-island journeys need separate arrangements; boat, ship, and small-aircraft options depend on the destination and conditions. Settle permissions, provisions, and the return journey with local contacts well ahead.</p><a class="block py-4 text-sm underline underline-offset-4" href={s.outerIslands}>Official outer-island planning guide <Icon name="arrow" /></a><a class="block py-4 text-sm underline underline-offset-4" href={s.tourismContact}>Ask the Pohnpei Tourism Office <Icon name="arrow" /></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="px-6 py-8 bg-sand-bright"><p class="tg-wrap text-sm text-basalt/75 leading-relaxed">PohnpeiIsland.com is an independent guide with no formal tourism-office affiliation. Route information comes from the linked tourism, aviation, and airline sources. Confirm operational details directly with your airline; bookings take place with the provider.</p></div>
</TravelGuideLayout>
